.TH APER 1 "July 26, 2026" "aper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aper \- render Penrose tilings as PDF
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aper
.RB [ \-t " p2|p3" ]
.RB [ \-s " seed" ]
.RB [ \-c " scheme" ]
.RB [ \-n " depth" ]
.br
.BR aper " " { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.BR aper " " { \-V | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aper
generates a finite P2 kite-and-dart or P3 rhomb Penrose tiling from a selected
starting design by Robinson subdivision and writes a complete native vector PDF
to standard output.
Diagnostics are written to standard error, so the PDF can be redirected or
piped without contamination.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tiling " " type
Select
.B p2
for kite-and-dart tiles or
.B p3
for thin and thick rhombs.
The default is
.BR p3 .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seed " " seed
Select the starting design.
P2 provides
.BR sun ,
.BR star ,
.BR ace ,
.BR deuce ,
.BR jack ,
.BR queen ,
and
.BR king .
P3 provides
.BR sun ,
.BR star ,
.BR thin ,
and
.BR thick .
The default is
.BR sun .
The P3
.B thin
seed requires a depth of at least 2.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-colour " " scheme
Select one of the
.BR flare ,
.BR grove ,
.BR electric ,
or
.B tide
colour schemes.
The default is
.BR flare .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-depth " " depth
Set the number of subdivisions to an integer from 1 through 12.
The default is 7.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a concise help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render the default tiling and open it:
.PP
.EX
aper > tiling.pdf
open tiling.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render a P2 queen patch using the electric colour scheme:
.PP
.EX
aper -t p2 -s queen -c electric -n 5 > queen.pdf
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B aper
exits zero after writing a complete PDF document and non-zero if its arguments
are invalid or output fails.
